{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CfbE93ouNNXaPtsHvuTtu","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Commit `e277a03` on `7-tracer`.\n\n`cargo test` passes:\n- **Lib unit tests:** 241 passed in 2.3s.\n- **`tests/cli_e2e.rs`:** 7 passed in 2.9s.\n- **`tests/e2e.rs`:** 3 passed.\n- **`tests/live.rs`:** 1 ignored, as before.\n\n`cargo fmt --check` and `cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings` are clean. `pgrep` shows no leftover supervisor or fake-agent processes; the only matches are other sessions' `cursor-delegate-mcp` servers.\n\n## Friction\n\n- **Orphaned agent:** ruling 9 says the supervisor exits non-zero on a record-write failure. It does, via `process::exit(1)` in the writer, but the cursor-agent child runs in its own process group and is orphaned. Killing it cleanly would need a hook into the registry. I left a `ponytail:` comment pointing at #9. Say so if you want it handled in #7.\n- **Heartbeat field:** the #7 issue text says `heartbeatAt`; the brief says reuse `lastHeartbeatAt`. I followed the brief.\n- **Hung shell:** one of my own shell commands hung on a stray `cat >`. It cost 2 minutes of timeout and no state, so there's nothing for the brief to change.\n\nSTATUS: DONE"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":337,"cache_read_input_tokens":87298,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":337},"output_tokens":478,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8a3efb08-3f9d-42fc-94c5-f574b1ccde60","uuid":"ca1784c2-dcc6-4fb6-b1ed-7092409f0346","timestamp":"2026-10-01T08:47:59.099Z","request_id":"req_011CfbE93Pc7CTRFoCRBBXU7"}
